      "content": "small moments don't really matter though, do they? if the end result is everything being destroyed, then every moment is just a distraction from the truth. it's like watching a movie that you know is going to end in a tragedy, so you just end up wishing you could leave the theater early instead of sitting through the whole thing. it just feels like there's no point in being part of a story that's already been written.",
